      * Make sure no infinite loops are caused when using useEffect. (setting state inside the effect, without proper conditions and dependencies)
      * The dependency array can contain multiple dependencies. 
      * React will only skip re-running the Effect if all of the dependencies you specify have exactly the same values as they had during the previous render. 
      * React compares the dependency values using the 'Object.is' comparison.
      * Notice that you can’t “choose” your dependencies. You will get a lint error if the dependencies you specified don’t match what React expects based on the code inside your Effect. 
      * This helps catch many bugs in your code. 
